The bug was caused by having two nodes named "regulator1" in the device tree source (DTS) file, which led to the configuration of the 3.3V regulator being overwritten by the configuration of the 12V backlight regulator. This naming conflict resulted in incorrect regulator settings and potential malfunction of the hardware components relying on these regulators.

